# Copy to .deploy.env at the repository root. .deploy.env is gitignored.
#
# IT DOES NOT TRAVEL BETWEEN CHECKOUTS. Git never carries a gitignored file, so a
# new worktree starts without one even though the checkout it was branched from
# has it. On 2026-09-19 there were sixteen worktrees here and exactly two held a
# .deploy.env. The other fourteen could each have run ./deploy.sh and taken the
# live site off HTTPS; deploy.sh now refuses instead, which is why this file
# exists to be found.
#
# Both variables below are read by deploy.sh at the repo root, or TARGET can be
# passed as the first argument: ./deploy.sh root@<box-ip>

# The box, as ssh would take it. The Vultr instance's IPv4 is in the Vultr
# dashboard and in docs/handoffs/2026-09-19_domain-live-handoff.md.
TARGET=root@<box-ip>

# The live domain. REQUIRED — deploy.sh refuses to run without it.
#
# Every deploy rsyncs the repo's Caddyfile over /etc/caddy/Caddyfile, and this is
# the site address written into it. Get it wrong and Caddy asks Let's Encrypt for
# a certificate it cannot validate; leave it unset and there is no certificate at
# all. The apex A record points here, so this is the apex, with no scheme, no
# port and no trailing slash.
#
# It is safetospend.STUDY. safetospend.us was the name originally chosen and it
# was never registered — .us does not permit WHOIS privacy — so it is NXDOMAIN
# and ACME on it fails. Some older handoffs still say .us; they are superseded.
DOMAIN=safetospend.study

# For a bare-IP smoke test with no certificate, do not blank DOMAIN — that is
# refused on purpose. Ask for it on the command line, once, where it is visible:
#
#   ./deploy.sh --no-domain
